context": {"bytes": {"conversation": 100628, "other": 423, "system": 37779, "tool_definitions": 14397, "tool_results": 49126}, "measure": "json-utf8-bytes", "total_bytes": 202353}, "gateway_set": ["thinking.display"], "web_search": false, "web_searches": 0, "calls": {"Bash": 1}}}, {"id": "2ff80bed-7549-527c-a67c-d9ccddd336ef", "at": 1795646973.3570304, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 71259, "layer": "worker", "category": "usage", "kind": "session.usage", "role": "idea-repo", "actor": "idea-repo", "execution_id": "dc1535ee578d0b4b7de35c676fe287ab", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "usage", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "context usage"}, {"id": "b0f9becc-444f-56c6-a6c1-5aed7d7182c5", "at": 1795646973.3638608, "until": 1795646976.2666545, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 71260, "layer": "worker", "category": "execute", "kind": "tool.pending", "role": "idea-repo", "actor": "idea-repo", "execution_id": "dc1535ee578d0b4b7de35c676fe287ab", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": "completed", "label": "execute → completed", "repository": null, "tool_call_id": "toolu_012DvT4kfdzeyFKx5jMSZEo3", "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "cd /hutian/paper && git fetch -q origin && git log --oneline -3 origin/candidate-v1; git diff f1030cd origin/candidate-v1 --stat -- paper refs | tail -8; git diff f1030cd origin/candidate-v1 -- paper/related.tex paper/design.tex | grep '^[…", "shown": {"trace": {"input": [["command", "cd /hutian/paper && git fetch -q origin && git log --oneline -3 origin/candidate-v1; git diff f1030cd origin/candidate-v1 --stat -- paper refs | tail -8; git diff f1030cd origin/candidate-v1 -- paper/related.tex paper/design.tex | grep '^[+-]' | cut -c1-500"]], "output": "```console\nff8fd08 Hedge the absence claim in related work; cite datasets and packages\n1f50799 Figures: caption_ranges.json (ranges for captions from the plotted csv); figures/tables rebuilt on results at 7d34633, otherwise unchanged\n5677d2d refs: full scikit-learn author list\n paper/design.tex  | 6 +++---\n paper/related.tex | 2 +-\n refs/refs.bib     | 4 ++--\n 3 files changed, 6 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)\n--- a/paper/design.tex\n+++ b/paper/design.tex\n-We use five public binary-classification tables, chosen to span the number of players $d$: German Credit ($d=20$, 1000 rows), ACS Employment ($d=16$) and ACS Income ($d=10$) from the 2018 one-year person file for California \\citep{ding2021}, Pima Indians Diabetes ($d=8$) and Give Me Some Credit ($d=10$).\n-For each dataset we fit logistic regression (LR), a random forest (RF, 100 trees, minimum leaf size 5), gradient boosting (XGBoost, 200 trees, depth 4) and a scikit-learn MLP (one hidden layer of $32$ units below $5000$ training rows, two of $64$ otherwise), on one train/test split; training sets are capped at 30\\,000 rows.\n+We use five public binary-classification tables, chosen to span the number of players $d$: German Credit \\citep{hofmann1994german} ($d=20$, 1000 rows), ACS Employment ($d=16$) and ACS Income ($d=10$) from the 2018 one-year person file for California \\citep{ding2021}, Pima Indians Diabetes \\citep{smith1988pima} ($d=8$) and Give Me Some Credit \\citep{gmsc2011} ($d=10$).\n+For each dataset we fit logistic regression (LR), a random forest (RF, 100 trees, minimum leaf size 5), gradient boosting (XGBoost \\citep{chen2016xgboost}, 200 trees, depth 4) and a scikit-learn \\citep{pedregosa2011sklearn} MLP (one hidden layer of $32$ units below $5000$ training rows, two of $64$ otherwise), on one train/test split; training sets are capped at 30\\,000 rows.\n-We run (i) the unchanged \\texttt{KernelExplainer} of the \\texttt{shap} package (version 0.51.0) with its default sampling, with \\texttt{l1\\_reg} set to \\texttt{False}, \\texttt{\"auto\"} (the default) and \\texttt{\"num\\_features(10)\"}; (ii) unbiased paired Kernel SHAP \\citep{covert2021}; and (iii) antithetic permutation sampling \\citep{mitchell2022}.\n+We run (i) the unchanged \\texttt{KernelExplainer} of the \\texttt{shap} package \\citep{lundberg2017} (version 0.51.0) with its default sampling, with \\texttt{l1\\_reg} set to \\texttt{False}, \\texttt{\"auto\"} (the default) and \\texttt{\"num\\_features(10)\"}; (ii) unbiased paired Kernel SHAP \\citep{covert2021}; and (iii) antithetic permutation sampling \\citep{mitchell2022}.\n--- a/paper/related.tex\n+++ b/paper/related.tex\n-They do not ask whether one run at a deployment budget supports the conclusion a reader draws from it for a given instance, nor whether the run can detect its own failure.\n+To our knowledge, in the sources we reviewed, they do not ask whether one run at a deployment budget supports the conclusion a reader draws from it for a given instance, or whether the run can detect its own failure.\n\nShell cwd was reset to /hutian/repo\n```", "exit": null}}}, {"id": "6e94a2a7-ec68-5618-9b22-9a48679106fe", "at": 1795646974.6113887, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 71263, "layer": "worker", "category": "usage", "kind": "session.usage", "role": "idea-repo", "actor": "idea-repo", "execution_id": "dc1535ee578d0b4b7de35c676fe287ab", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "usage", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "context usage"}, {"id": "20610aa3-f58e-513f-9ec9-23da1e16c140", "at": 1795646974.65519, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 71264, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.session/request_permission", "role": "idea-repo", "actor": "idea-repo", "execution_id": "dc1535ee578d0b4b7de35c676fe287ab", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "session/request_permission"}, {"id": "8efb711d-4ccc-51cc-987c-f8a5cf8c6ea2", "at": 1795646974.6598327, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 71265, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.response", "role": 